  m_Name: Toadstool
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  mushroomname: 'Toadstool '
  mushroominfor: "The Toadstool, with its iconic red cap speckled with white warts,
    is the fairytale star of Finnish forests. Often found nestled among birch and
    pine, these mushrooms bring a whimsical touch to the woodland floor. However,
    their beauty is deceptive\u2014while mesmerizing to look at, Toadstools are toxic
    and not for eating. Historically, they\u2019ve played roles in folklore and traditional
    practices, but for modern foragers, they serve more as a reminder of nature\u2019s
    balance between allure and danger. Admire them from afar, but keep them out of
    your basket!"
  image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 3cc736ec3493add4bb1c25e0d7c582af, type: 3}
  mushroomtype: 1
